    operand overlap: 4-12 pixels
    if duplicate operand copies create ambiguous triples, all share the same destination
  distractors: remaining 3 sprites must NOT form any additional union triple with a different destination
  output:
    same grid, same layout
    operand sprites a,b recolored teal (color 8)
    destination sprite d recolored green (color 3)
    other 3 sprites remain red
    no structural changes, only color substitution

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Create two random non-empty 4x4 binary masks (operands a, b) such that each has >=1 unique pixel and their union is non-trivial (not identical to either operand).
    2. Compute destination mask d = a | b.
    3. Generate 3 distractor 4x4 masks randomly. Validate that no pair of {a, b, d0, d1, d2} unions to any other member (or if so, only with same destination d). Reject and retry if violated.
    4. Shuffle all 6 sprites into a random permutation across the 3x2 grid positions.
    5. Build 16x11 grid: 1-row/col black margins, 1-row/col black gaps between cells. Place all masks as red pixels.
```
